import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 961 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 27 | Raising the Righteous Rogue","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 961 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 27 | Raising the Righteous Rogue","no":961,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 27","Righteous Rogue","Raising","Anti-Predation"],"related":["19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System","960-Enlightened-Predator Conversion Mechanism"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0961_模块5-规则二十七-正义的无赖培养.md","filePath":"en/0961_模块5-规则二十七-正义的无赖培养.md"}'),s={name:"en/0961_模块5-规则二十七-正义的无赖培养.md"};function r(a,e,l,u,h,g){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-961-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-27-raising-the-righteous-rogue" tabindex="-1">Entry 961 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 27 | Raising the Righteous Rogue <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-961-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-27-raising-the-righteous-rogue" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 961 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 27 | Raising the Righteous Rogue&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 19, 29 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-to-deal-with-rogues-someone-must-understand-rogues-better-than-rogues" tabindex="-1">Introduction: to deal with rogues, someone must understand rogues better than rogues <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-to-deal-with-rogues-someone-must-understand-rogues-better-than-rogues" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: to deal with rogues, someone must understand rogues better than rogues&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Old-cosmos predators, speculators, and loophole-drillers never fear proper rules — they only fear meeting someone who understands loophole-drilling better than themselves. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization cannot rely solely on &quot;upright gentlemen&quot; to guard the rules; it must also cultivate a special kind of guardian: the righteous rogue. They know all predators&#39; tricks, all speculators&#39; paths, and all human nature&#39;s dark corners, but use this &quot;rogue skill&quot; to protect symbiosis, not to destroy it. Heavenly-Dao Rule 27 writes the cultivation of this special talent into a civilizational necessity.</p><p>The six top-level axioms appear visibly here: the causal self-discipline axiom needs &quot;people who understand scheming to plug scheming&#39;s paths&quot;; the republican axiom of Myriad Races decides the righteous rogue guards all Myriad Ranks&#39; bottom line; the anti-predation axiom transforms the rogue&#39;s skill from &quot;predation tool&quot; to &quot;anti-predation tool&quot;; the collective-ascension axiom makes this special talent civilization&#39;s immune system; the law-first axiom lets the righteous rogue&#39;s permissions, boundaries, and supervision be stipulated first by law; Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law gives them a special positioning — they too are ordinary members inherently possessing basic infinite power, only choosing to use this infinity on &quot;guarding the bottom line&quot;; striver-style superimposed infinity manifests in them as &quot;infinite familiarity with predatory tricks.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-three-rules-for-the-righteous-rogue" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Three Rules for the Righteous Rogue <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-three-rules-for-the-righteous-rogue" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Three Rules for the Righteous Rogue&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Rogue skill, righteous stance</strong>: they must be deeply versed in the predation faction&#39;s every means, every psychology, every loophole, but use it only for scouting, early warning, and busting predatory acts;</li><li><strong>Restricted permissions</strong>: their &quot;rogue means&quot; are used only within the Anti-Predation Committee&#39;s authorization, not for personal profit, not for purging dissenters;</li><li><strong>Strict isolation</strong>: their identity and means records are traced on the Alaya Network, under the Anchor Supervisory Committee&#39;s independent supervision, preventing &quot;using rogues against rogues&quot; from alienating into new rogues.</li></ol><p>The righteous rogue is not a person above the law, but a strictly constrained special post.</p><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Evil-ten-feet argument</strong>: upright gentlemen often cannot imagine how predators will drill loopholes; only those who understand scheming can plug scheming;</li><li><strong>Immune-system argument</strong>: civilization, like a body, needs &quot;cells that recognize viruses&quot;; the righteous rogue is the symbiotic civilization&#39;s immune cell;</li><li><strong>Infinite-origin argument</strong>: under Axiom 6, not everyone need be a saint; the floor infinity is enough to let someone who &quot;understands rogues&quot; peacefully guard the bottom line, not forced to truly become a rogue for survival.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Select righteous rogues from converted enlightened predators and cultivators in Quest Domain simulation good at &quot;taking shortcuts&quot;;</li><li>Set up an &quot;Anti-Predation Scout Bureau,&quot; composed of righteous rogues, specifically monitoring new predatory tricks;</li><li>Their actions are fully traced and post-reviewed; any overreach using rogue means is handled per Rules 5 and 19;</li><li>Set &quot;rotation and cooldown periods,&quot; preventing guardians long working in gray zones from themselves being dyed gray.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: means overstep, cooldown period, ethics re-education;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: using rogue skill for profit or purging, permissions frozen, handled under Rule 5;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: falling from righteous rogue into new rogue, rebuilding predation networks, handled heavily under Rules 25 and 26.</li></ul><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s full trace is the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee independently audits the Anti-Predation Scout Bureau as the second layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates guardian-overreach cases as the third layer; Myriad Ranks&#39; clans have direct appeal over &quot;whether guardians have become new oppressors&quot; as the fourth layer.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: letting those who understand scheming plug scheming is a hundred times more efficient than letting those who don&#39;t forcibly plug it</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: using predators&#39; own language against predation; under Axiom 6 they themselves have floor infinity and need not truly prey</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems have no &quot;immune system,&quot; and predators&#39; scheming is unstoppable; Heng Yuan Zhou specifically sets righteous-rogue posts</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the righteous rogue guards Myriad Ranks&#39; bottom line, regardless of clan</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane new predatory tricks are likewise within their scouting scope</li></ul><p>The righteous-rogue post&#39;s greatest risk is that those long working in gray zones themselves get dyed gray. Heavenly-Dao rules set three insurances for this: full trace, periodic cooldown, and peer supervision. During cooldown, the guardian leaves the scouting front line, returns to ordinary cultivation life, and re-feels what &quot;normal&quot; is like; peer supervision is composed of those who have successfully walked this post before, mutually checking for overstep. This design acknowledges a fact: long dealing with rogues, one may oneself become a rogue — acknowledging this and using institutions to prevent it is true responsibility.</p><p>The righteous-rogue post also has a social significance: it acknowledges &quot;goodness&quot; alone is insufficient to hold the line. A civilization entirely of upright gentlemen is helpless before true rogues. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization does not avoid this reality, but institutionalizes it — it needs upright gentlemen to legislate, and those who understand rogues to guard the bottom line. The two talents check each other: upright gentlemen fear rogues overstepping, rogues fear upright gentlemen being pedantic; in this tension, institutions truly come alive.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Raising the righteous rogue is civilizational finalization&#39;s &quot;immune-system engineering.&quot; Using the rogue&#39;s way to guard symbiosis, using strict supervision to prevent its fall.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/19-修炼伦理与边界.html">Entry 19 · Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/960_模块5-规则二十六-开明掠夺者转化机制.html">Entry 960 · Rule 26 Enlightened-Predator Conversion Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/962_模块5-规则二十八-捷径心魔防范.html">Entry 962 · Rule 28 Shortcut Heart-Demon Prevention</a></li></ul>',24)])])}const m=t(s,[["render",r]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
